  "notes": "Cash-basis village. Governmental from Total Governmental Funds column (p4; General, Streets, Capital Improvement); balances are fund balances (begin 1,067,393, end 1,157,412), which include interfund due-from. Business-type (Water, Sewer) from proprietary statement p6, measure net position (deficit, cash basis); beginning/ending are net position, not cash. Balance sheet from the Statement of Net Position - Cash Basis total column (p1). Detail: General Fund combining schedule p7 (General and Park columns) recorded as the more detailed schedule for the General Fund (the p4 General column equals the p7 Total column); p8 all-funds budget schedule gives only broad groups mixing funds; recorded only lines belonging to a single fund not covered by p7: Water, Sewer and Debt Service (business-type) and Public Works 30,454 and Capital Outlay 13,208 (both entirely Streets fund per p4); its receipt groups and General government mix funds and were not recorded, to avoid double counting; no detail_totals for p8. p8 totals tie to gov + business-type statements (receipts 731,722; disbursements 640,490). Interfund transfers 25,152 are within the General Fund (General to Park) per p4. Trimmed PDF pages: p1 report p4, p2 p5, p3 p6, p4 p7, p5 p8, p6 p9, p7 p21, p8 p22. Read pages 1-8 of 8. Statement of Activities - Cash Basis (p2, added by v8 re-trim) checked: governmental general receipts 387,658, program receipts 39,233, disbursements 336,872 and business-type change 1,213 agree with the fund statements; nothing new recorded from it to avoid double counting. Streets fund General government 2,341 (p4 Streets column) added to detail so Streets spending is complete (2,341 + 30,454 + 13,208 = 46,003); Streets and Capital Improvement receipts have no fund-level supplementary schedule (p8 receipt groups mix funds) and stay only in the statement receipts.",
